<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32238" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏcŭlo</span></b> , 1,
			v. a.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To furnish with eyes</i>, <i>make to
				see</i> (eccl. Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pullos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Poen. 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to enlighten</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homines in agnitionem veritatis oculare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caecos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cypr. Idol. Van. 7, 6</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To make visible</i> or <i>conspicuous</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestem purpurā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pud. 8</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
